From the same revision and license, these PNGs were replaced with their 300x300 versions. The
snapshot's references were flattened onto white: their opaque seagreen interiors were stored as
(0, 113, 49) at alpha 209, which matches only when composited over white. Their SVG inputs are
byte-identical at both revisions. The snapshot's subregion-and-primitiveUnits=objectBoundingBox-1
and -2 references are flattened the same way but are kept: the v0.49.0 renderings end their
0.5-wide objectBoundingBox subregion at 98 user units instead of the 84 that the element's
bounding box gives, which the snapshot and Donner both draw. The snapshot's
everything-via-xlink-href, some-attributes-via-xlink-href and with-region-and-subregion
references are flattened too but are kept: their filter regions cut the blur's input, and the
v0.49.0 renderings drop the box-blur spill there, which Donner keeps.

